  "output": "## Test Coverage Analysis — Canon (web)\n\n**Headline finding: this repo has zero test infrastructure.** No test runner is installed (`package.json` has no `jest`/`vitest`/`playwright`/`@testing-library/*`), no `*.test.*`/`*.spec.*` files exist anywhere, and there's no CI test step to enforce coverage going forward. Coverage is 0% across ~30 source files in `lib/`, `lib/server/`, `app/api/`, and `components/`.\n\nBefore anything else, this needs a harness. Recommended: **Vitest** (fast, ESM-native, works well with Next 16 + React 19 Server Components split) + `@testing-library/react` for the handful of client components/hooks. Add:\n\n```bash\nnpm i -D vitest @vitejs/plugin-react @testing-library/react @testing-library/jest-dom jsdom\n```\n\n```ts\n// vitest.config.ts\nimport { defineConfig } from \"vitest/config\";\nimport react from \"@vitejs/plugin-react\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [react()],\n  test: {\n    environment: \"jsdom\",\n    setupFiles: [\"./vitest.setup.ts\"],\n  },\n  resolve: { alias: { \"@\": path.resolve(__dirname, \".\") } },\n});\n```\n\n```json\n// package.json scripts\n\"test\": \"vitest run\",\n\"test:watch\": \"vitest\"\n```\n\nEverything below assumes this setup. Findings are grouped by ROI: pure functions first (no mocking, highest value), then DB-backed server modules, then API routes, then client-side.\n\n---\n\n### Tier 1 — Pure functions with zero test coverage (highest ROI)\n\nThese have no I/O, are exported, and encode real business rules (survivorship folding, diff rendering, run staging). They should be the first tests written.\n\n| File | Untested exports | Notable edge cases |\n|---|---|---|\n| `lib/validate-value.ts` | `foldValue`, `checkObservedValue`, `observedValues` | multi-suffix stripping (`\"Trellis Labs Pvt Ltd\"`), suffix-only input (`\"Ltd\"`), empty candidate, both sides empty, exact match vs folded match, Unicode normalization (NFKD) |\n| `lib/diff-chars.ts` | `diffSegments` | equal strings, completely disjoint strings, one empty string, prefix+suffix overlap (`\"aa\"` vs `\"a\"`) |\n| `lib/format.ts` | `shortRunId`, `formatElapsed`, `formatCount`, `formatStat`, `formatClockTime`, `formatTimestamp`, `formatRelative`, `formatConfidence` | hour rollover in `formatElapsed`, negative ms, `null`/`undefined` in `formatStat`, boundary seconds in `formatRelative` (59s/60s, 23h/24h) |\n| `lib/rule-trace.ts` | `deriveRuleTrace` | no resolution yet, rule decided vs. model proposed, escalated (no value), rule decided but no strategy found |\n| `lib/reviewer-label.ts` | `reviewerLabel` | null user, username present, only email present, neither present (fallback) |\n| `lib/audit-detail.ts` | `auditDetailParts`, `auditDetailLine`, `auditNote` | empty detail object, `from === to` (no arrow), only `to`, only `from`, unknown `action` (no noun), non-string/non-number malformed detail values |\n| `lib/uuid.ts` | `isUuid` | uppercase UUID, malformed segments, extra characters |\n| `types/queue.ts` | `conflictFieldLabel`, `severityReason` | orphan, duplicate with `to === 0` vs `to > 0`, singular vs plural child count, unknown conflict class (default branch) |\n| `types/run.ts` | `isTerminalRunStatus`, `runStageIndex`, `isStatKnown`, `failedStage`, `RUN_STAGES` | `failed` status (`runStageIndex` → -1), stat not yet produced vs. produced, failed run stat visibility, `failedStage` with no `stage=` in error, case-insensitive verb match, unknown verb |\n| `lib/server/export.ts` | `decisionsToCsv`, `estimateExportBytes`, `isExportSection` | CSV escaping (commas, quotes, newlines in a value), `null` cells, empty decision list |\n\n**Skeletons:**\n\n```ts\n// lib/validate-value.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { foldValue, checkObservedValue, observedValues } from \"@/lib/validate-value\";\n\ndescribe(\"foldValue\", () => {\n  it(\"folds case, punctuation and whitespace\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"ACME-INC\")).toBe(foldValue(\"ACME INC\"));\n  });\n\n  it(\"strips a single legal suffix\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Acme Corp\")).toBe(\"acme\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"strips multiple stacked suffixes, longest match first\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Trellis Labs Pvt Ltd\")).toBe(\"trellis labs\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"keeps a value that IS entirely a suffix\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Ltd\")).toBe(\"ltd\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"is idempotent and total for empty input\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"\")).toBe(\"\");\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"checkObservedValue\", () => {\n  const observed = [\"Acme Inc.\", \"ACME INC\"];\n\n  it(\"accepts an exact match\", () => {\n    const result = checkObservedValue(\"Acme Inc.\", observed);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ ok: true, matches: \"Acme Inc.\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"accepts a legal normalization of an observed value\", () => {\n    const result = checkObservedValue(\"acme inc\", observed);\n    expect(result.ok).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects a value neither side holds\", () => {\n    const result = checkObservedValue(\"Globex\", observed);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ ok: false, reason: expect.stringContaining(\"Must be one of\") });\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects an empty/whitespace-only candidate\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"   \", observed).ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects when neither side has a real value (orphan)\", () => {\n    const result = checkObservedValue(\"anything\", [\"\", \"  \"]);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ ok: false, reason: expect.stringContaining(\"Neither side\") });\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"observedValues\", () => {\n  it(\"flattens and drops blank entries from both sides\", () => {\n    const row = { a: { values: [\"x\", \"\"] }, b: { values: [\"y\"] } };\n    expect(observedValues(row)).toEqual([\"x\", \"y\"]);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```ts\n// types/run.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { isStatKnown, failedStage, runStageIndex, isTerminalRunStatus } from \"@/types/run\";\n\ndescribe(\"isStatKnown\", () => {\n  it(\"is unknown before its producing stage has finished\", () => {\n    expect(isStatKnown(\"matches\", \"extracting\")).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"is known once the producing stage is behind current status\", () => {\n    expect(isStatKnown(\"matches\", \"detecting\")).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  it(\"is known for every stat once complete\", () => {\n    expect(isStatKnown(\"tokensUsed\", \"complete\")).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  it(\"is known for every stat when failed, regardless of where it died\", () => {\n    expect(isStatKnown(\"escalated\", \"failed\")).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"failedStage\", () => {\n  it(\"returns null when the error carries no stage= marker\", () => {\n    expect(failedStage(\"connection reset\")).toBeNull();\n  });\n\n  it(\"maps a known verb to its RunStage, case-insensitively\", () => {\n    expect(failedStage(\"source=Databricks GTM STAGE=Extract\")).toBe(\"extracting\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns null for an unrecognized verb\", () => {\n    expect(failedStage(\"stage=teleport\")).toBeNull();\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns null for a null error\", () => {\n    expect(failedStage(null)).toBeNull();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"runStageIndex / isTerminalRunStatus\", () => {\n  it(\"failed has no position in the pipeline\", () => {\n    expect(runStageIndex(\"failed\")).toBe(-1);\n  });\n\n  it(\"complete and failed are the only terminal states\", () => {\n    expect(isTerminalRunStatus(\"complete\")).toBe(true);\n    expect(isTerminalRunStatus(\"failed\")).toBe(true);\n    expect(isTerminalRunStatus(\"resolving\")).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```ts\n// lib/server/export.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { decisionsToCsv, type DecisionRow } from \"@/lib/server/export\";\n\nconst row: DecisionRow = {\n  conflictId: \"c1\", externalId: \"ACC-1\", entityName: \"Acme, Inc.\", entityType: \"account\",\n  field: \"name\", valueA: \"Acme\", valueB: \"Acme Inc\", conflictClass: \"cosmetic\", severity: 1,\n  detectedBy: \"rule\", status: \"approved\", proposedValue: \"Acme\", overrideValue: null,\n  appliedValue: \"Acme\", appliedRuleId: \"r1\", confidence: 0.9, rationale: \"most_recent\",\n  reviewedBy: \"j.rao\", reviewedAt: \"2026-08-06T18:02:00.000Z\",\n};\n\ndescribe(\"decisionsToCsv\", () => {\n  it(\"quotes and escapes cells containing commas or quotes\", () => {\n    const csv = decisionsToCsv([row]);\n    expect(csv).toContain('\"Acme, Inc.\"');\n  });\n\n  it(\"emits a header row plus CRLF-terminated rows, ending with a trailing CRLF\", () => {\n    const csv = decisionsToCsv([row]);\n    expect(csv.endsWith(\"\\r\\n\")).toBe(true);\n    expect(csv.split(\"\\r\\n\")[0]).toContain(\"conflictId\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"renders null cells as empty strings, not the literal 'null'\", () => {\n    const csv = decisionsToCsv([{ ...row, overrideValue: null }]);\n    expect(csv).not.toContain(\"null\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"handles an empty decision list (header only)\", () => {\n    expect(decisionsToCsv([]).trim().split(\"\\r\\n\")).toHaveLength(1);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### Tier 2 — Server data-access modules (need a mocked `db`)\n\nNone of `lib/server/*.ts` has a seam for injecting a fake DB today — `getDb()` is called directly inside each function. To unit-test these without a real Postgres instance, mock `@/lib/db`'s `getDb` with `vi.mock`. The highest-value target is **`recordReview`** in `lib/server/conflicts.ts` — it's the one function with real branching business logic (four distinct rejection paths) sitting on top of writes.\n\n```ts\n// lib/server/conflicts.recordReview.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi, beforeEach } from \"vitest\";\n\nconst mockDb = { update: vi.fn(), select: vi.fn(), /* ...chain stubs */ };\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/db\", () => ({ getDb: () => mockDb }));\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/server/audit\", () => ({ appendAudit: vi.fn() }));\n\nimport { recordReview } from \"@/lib/server/conflicts\";\n\ndescribe(\"recordReview\", () => {\n  beforeEach(() => vi.clearAllMocks());\n\n  it(\"returns 404 when the conflict does not exist\", async () => {\n    // arrange getReviewTarget's underlying query to resolve to []\n    const result = await recordReview({ conflictId: \"missing\", action: { action: \"approve\" }, reviewer: { userId: \"u1\", label: \"j.rao\" } });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ ok: false, code: 404, message: expect.any(String) });\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns 409 when nothing has been proposed yet (run still resolving)\", async () => {\n    // arrange target with resolution: null\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns 409 approving an escalated conflict with an empty proposedValue\", async () => {\n    // arrange resolution.proposedValue === \"\" and action.action === \"approve\"\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns 400 when override value is not an observed value\", async () => {\n    // arrange target.observed = [\"A\", \"B\"], action.overrideValue = \"C\"\n  });\n\n  it(\"folds an override onto its matched observed value before writing\", async () => {\n    // assert db.update(...).set({ overrideValue: <folded match>, ... })\n  });\n\n  it(\"clears overrideValue when action is approve/reject\", async () => {\n    // assert set({ overrideValue: null })\n  });\n\n  it(\"appends an audit row with previousStatus set to the prior resolution status\", async () => {\n    // assert appendAudit called with detail.previousStatus\n  });\n});\n```\n\nOther server modules needing at least basic coverage (mock `getDb`, assert query shape / return mapping, not Drizzle internals):\n\n- **`lib/server/engine.ts`** — `startRun`/`fetchEngineStatus` are the best integration-test candidates in the whole repo because they're pure `fetch` wrappers: mock `global.fetch`.\n  - `startRun`: `ENGINE_URL` unset → throws `EngineUnreachableError` before fetching; fetch throws (network) → wrapped error; fetch rejects with non-timeout `Error`; `AbortSignal.timeout` fires → message says \"no response within Ns\"; non-ok response → error includes truncated body; ok response with malformed JSON body → contract-break error; ok response but body fails `engineStartRunResponseSchema` → contract-break error.\n  - `fetchEngineStatus`: non-ok response → `null` (not throw); malformed JSON → `null`; fetch throws → `null`; valid response → parsed data returned.\n\n```ts\n// lib/server/engine.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi, beforeEach, afterEach } from \"vitest\";\nimport { startRun, fetchEngineStatus, EngineUnreachableError } from \"@/lib/server/engine\";\n\ndescribe(\"startRun\", () => {\n  const originalEnv = process.env.ENGINE_URL;\n  beforeEach(() => { process.env.ENGINE_URL = \"http://engine.local\"; });\n  afterEach(() => { process.env.ENGINE_URL = originalEnv; vi.restoreAllMocks(); });\n\n  it(\"throws EngineUnreachableError when ENGINE_URL is unset\", async () => {\n    delete process.env.ENGINE_URL;\n    await expect(startRun(\"run-1\")).rejects.toThrow(EngineUnreachableError);\n  });\n\n  it(\"wraps a network failure\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockRejectedValue(new Error(\"ECONNREFUSED\")));\n    await expect(startRun(\"run-1\")).rejects.toThrow(/Engine did not accept the run/);\n  });\n\n  it(\"throws with response status + truncated body on non-ok\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(\n      new Response(\"internal error details...\", { status: 500 }),\n    ));\n    await expect(startRun(\"run-1\")).rejects.toThrow(/rejected the run with 500/);\n  });\n\n  it(\"throws a contract-break error when the 200 body doesn't match the schema\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(\n      Response.json({ unexpected: true }, { status: 200 }),\n    ));\n    await expect(startRun(\"run-1\")).rejects.toThrow(/unexpected body/);\n  });\n\n  it(\"resolves on a well-formed 200\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(\n      Response.json({ runId: \"run-1\", accepted: true }, { status: 200 }),\n    ));\n    await expect(startRun(\"run-1\")).resolves.toBeUndefined();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"fetchEngineStatus\", () => {\n  it(\"returns null (not throw) when the engine responds non-ok\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(new Response(null, { status: 503 })));\n    await expect(fetchEngineStatus(\"run-1\")).resolves.toBeNull();\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns null when fetch itself throws (engine unreachable)\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockRejectedValue(new Error(\"timeout\")));\n    await expect(fetchEngineStatus(\"run-1\")).resolves.toBeNull();\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns null when the body fails schema validation\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(Response.json({ bogus: true })));\n    await expect(fetchEngineStatus(\"run-1\")).resolves.toBeNull();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n- **`lib/server/sources.ts`** — `countSourcesBySide` classification (`salesforce`/`hubspot` → crm, `databricks`/`snowflake` → warehouse, `synthetic` → synthetic); `findSourceIds` with empty array (must short-circuit, not query); `findSourceIds` with ids that don't exist.\n- **`lib/server/runs.ts`** — `getSeverityBreakdown` dropping a severity value outside 1–4 (engine-bug defense); `failUndispatchedRun` only updates rows still `queued` (guard against overwriting engine progress) — this needs an integration-level test against a real/test DB since the guard is expressed as a WHERE clause, not app logic.\n- **`lib/server/rulesets.ts`** — `createRulesetVersion`: first version for a brand-new name (`highest` is `null` → version 1); concurrent-save serialization via advisory lock (integration test only); exactly one active ruleset invariant after save.\n- **`lib/server/entities.ts`** — `countChildrenByParent` with empty `externalIds` (must short-circuit); dedup of duplicate ids in input.\n- **`lib/server/export.ts`** — `buildRunExport`: requesting `hierarchy` alone still loads decisions internally (dependency) but the response omits the `decisions` key; empty `sections` array; `applyDecisions`/reparenting logic (currently unexported — consider exporting for direct unit testing rather than only through `buildRunExport`).\n- **`lib/server/audit.ts`** — this is explicitly append-only; a good regression test is asserting **no** `update`/`delete` call ever appears in this module (a grep-based or explicit \"no such export\" test), since that invariant is stated in the file's own comment as load-bearing.\n\n---\n\n### Tier 3 — API routes (missing almost entirely; these are the integration-test gap)\n\nEvery route in `app/api/**/route.ts` is currently exercised by nothing. Use `next/server`'s `Request`/`Response` directly (no need for a running server) with mocked `lib/server/*` modules.\n\n```ts\n// app/api/runs/route.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi, beforeEach } from \"vitest\";\n\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/server/auth\", () => ({ requireReviewer: vi.fn() }));\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/server/sources\", () => ({ findSourceIds: vi.fn() }));\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/server/rulesets\", () => ({ getRuleset: vi.fn() }));\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/server/runs\", () => ({ createRun: vi.fn(), failUndispatchedRun: vi.fn(), listRuns: vi.fn() }));\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/server/engine\", async (importOriginal) => ({\n  ...(await importOriginal<typeof import(\"@/lib/server/engine\")>()),\n  startRun: vi.fn(),\n}));\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/server/audit\", () => ({ appendAudit: vi.fn() }));\n\nimport { POST } from \"@/app/api/runs/route\";\n\nfunction req(body: unknown) {\n  return new Request(\"http://test/api/runs\", {\n    method: \"POST\",\n    headers: { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" },\n    body: JSON.stringify(body),\n  });\n}\n\ndescribe(\"POST /api/runs\", () => {\n  beforeEach(() => vi.clearAllMocks());\n\n  it(\"400s when the body fails Zod validation\", async () => {\n    const res = await POST(req({ sourceAId: \"not-a-uuid\" }));\n    expect(res.status).toBe(400);\n  });\n\n  it(\"400s when sourceAId === sourceBId\", async () => {\n    const id = \"11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111\";\n    const res = await POST(req({ sourceAId: id, sourceBId: id, rulesetId: id }));\n    expect(res.status).toBe(400);\n    expect((await res.json()).error).toMatch(/must be different/);\n  });\n\n  it(\"400s when sourceAId no longer exists\", async () => { /* findSourceIds mock returns Set without it */ });\n  it(\"400s when the ruleset no longer exists\", async () => { /* getRuleset mock resolves null */ });\n\n  it(\"still returns 201 with the run id when the engine dispatch fails\", async () => {\n    // startRun mock rejects with EngineUnreachableError\n    // assert failUndispatchedRun + appendAudit(\"run_failed\") both called\n    // assert response status 201 (run row is real even though dispatch failed)\n  });\n\n  it(\"propagates a non-EngineUnreachableError from startRun instead of swallowing it\", async () => {\n    // startRun mock rejects with a plain Error — should NOT be caught\n  });\n\n  it(\"201s and returns { runId } on the happy path\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n```\n\n```ts\n// app/api/conflicts/[conflictId]/resolution/route.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi } from \"vitest\";\n\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/server/auth\", () => ({ requireReviewer: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({ userId: \"u1\", label: \"j.rao\" }) }));\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/server/conflicts\", () => ({ recordReview: vi.fn() }));\n\nimport { PATCH } from \"@/app/api/conflicts/[conflictId]/resolution/route\";\nimport { recordReview } from \"@/lib/server/conflicts\";\n\ndescribe(\"PATCH /api/conflicts/:conflictId/resolution\", () => {\n  it(\"404s immediately for a non-UUID conflictId, without touching the DB\", async () => {\n    const res = await PATCH(\n      new Request(\"http://t\", { method: \"PATCH\", body: \"{}\" }),\n      { params: Promise.resolve({ conflictId: \"not-a-uuid\" }) },\n    );\n    expect(res.status).toBe(404);\n    expect(recordReview).not.toHaveBeenCalled();\n  });\n\n  it(\"400s on a malformed action body (missing discriminant)\", async () => { /* ... */ });\n\n  it(\"returns recordReview's error code/message verbatim on failure\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(recordReview).mockResolvedValue({ ok: false, code: 409, message: \"already resolved\" });\n    // assert res.status === 409 and body.error === \"already resolved\"\n  });\n\n  it(\"never accepts a client-supplied reviewedBy — reviewer always comes from the session\", async () => {\n    // send a body with an extra \"reviewedBy\" field and assert it's ignored/stripped by the schema\n  });\n});\n```\n\nSame pattern applies to the remaining untested routes: `app/api/conflicts/route.ts`, `app/api/rulesets/route.ts`, `app/api/runs/[runId]/route.ts`, `app/api/runs/[runId]/status/route.ts`, `app/api/runs/[runId]/export/route.ts`, `app/api/audit/export/route.ts`, `app/api/sources/route.ts`. Common gaps across all of them worth checking explicitly:\n- Auth boundary: what happens if `requireReviewer()` throws (no session) — should surface, not be swallowed.\n- Malformed/non-JSON body → `parseJson` returns the `badRequest(\"Body must be JSON.\")` path — untested for every POST/PATCH route.\n- `app/api/_lib/respond.ts`'s `fieldIssues` — no direct unit test for how nested Zod paths get flattened (e.g. `config.objects` key formation, the `\"_\"` fallback key for a root-level issue).\n\n```ts\n// app/api/_lib/respond.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\nimport { parseJson, badRequest, notFound } from \"@/app/api/_lib/respond\";\n\ndescribe(\"parseJson\", () => {\n  it(\"returns badRequest when the body isn't valid JSON\", async () => {\n    const req = new Request(\"http://t\", { method: \"POST\", body: \"{not json\" });\n    const result = await parseJson(req, z.object({}));\n    expect(result.ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"flattens a nested path issue into a dotted key\", async () => {\n    const schema = z.object({ config: z.object({ objects: z.string() }) });\n    const req = new Request(\"http://t\", { method: \"POST\", body: JSON.stringify({ config: {} }) });\n    const result = await parseJson(req, schema);\n    if (!result.ok) {\n      const body = await result.response.json();\n      expect(body.issues).toHaveProperty(\"config.objects\");\n    }\n  });\n\n  it(\"uses '_' as the key for a root-level issue\", async () => { /* refine() at top level */ });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### Tier 4 — Client-side (hooks, components)\n\n- **`components/conflicts/use-review.ts`** — the one hook with real state logic and zero tests. With `@testing-library/react`'s `renderHook`:\n  - `submit` sets `pendingId` during the request and clears it after, on both success and failure.\n  - On success, `decided[conflictId]` reflects the server's returned status/reviewedBy (not an optimistic guess).\n  - On failure, `decided` is untouched and the returned result carries the server's message.\n  - `router.refresh()` is called (wrapped in `startTransition`) only on success, never on failure.\n\n```ts\n// components/conflicts/use-review.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi, beforeEach } from \"vitest\";\nimport { renderHook, act, waitFor } from \"@testing-library/react\";\n\nconst refresh = vi.fn();\nvi.mock(\"next/navigation\", () => ({ useRouter: () => ({ refresh }) }));\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/api-client\", () => ({ patchJson: vi.fn() }));\n\nimport { useReview } from \"@/components/conflicts/use-review\";\nimport { patchJson } from \"@/lib/api-client\";\n\ndescribe(\"useReview\", () => {\n  beforeEach(() => vi.clearAllMocks());\n\n  it(\"records the server-returned status on success and triggers a refresh\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(patchJson).mockResolvedValue({ ok: true, data: { conflictId: \"c1\", status: \"approved\", reviewedBy: \"j.rao\" } });\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useReview());\n\n    await act(async () => {\n      const outcome = await result.current.submit(\"c1\", { action: \"approve\" });\n      expect(outcome).toEqual({ ok: true });\n    });\n\n    expect(result.current.decided.c1).toEqual({ status: \"approved\", reviewedBy: \"j.rao\" });\n    await waitFor(() => expect(refresh).toHaveBeenCalled());\n  });\n\n  it(\"leaves decided untouched and returns the server message on failure\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(patchJson).mockResolvedValue({ ok: false, message: \"Nothing was proposed.\" });\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useReview());\n\n    await act(async () => {\n      const outcome = await result.current.submit(\"c1\", { action: \"approve\" });\n      expect(outcome).toEqual({ ok: false, message: \"Nothing was proposed.\" });\n    });\n\n    expect(result.current.decided.c1).toBeUndefined();\n    expect(refresh).not.toHaveBeenCalled();\n  });\n\n  it(\"clears pendingId after the request settles, even on failure\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(patchJson).mockResolvedValue({ ok: false, message: \"err\" });\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useReview());\n    await act(async () => { await result.current.submit(\"c1\", { action: \"reject\" }); });\n    expect(result.current.pendingId).toBeNull();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n- **`lib/api-client.ts`** (`postJson`/`patchJson` via `sendJson`) — currently untested and easy to cover with `vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", ...)`: network failure → generic \"Could not reach the server\" message; non-ok response with `{ error, issues }` body → surfaced verbatim; non-ok response with unparsable body → falls back to `Request failed (status)`; ok response → `{ ok: true, data }`.\n\n- Presentational components (`components/ui/*`, `components/runs/*`, `components/conflicts/*` non-hook files) have no tests either, but most are thin render/prop-passthrough — lower priority than the above unless a specific one has embedded logic (e.g. `severity-mark.tsx`, `conflict-diff-row.tsx` calling `diffSegments`). Worth a quick pass with React Testing Library only for components that branch on props (e.g. rendering `present: false` vs `true` on `ConflictSide`, or empty states like `sources-empty-state.tsx`).\n\n---\n\n### Missing error-handling tests (cross-cutting)\n\nThese are the specific failure paths that exist in the code but have no test anywhere:\n1. Engine unreachable at run start → run still gets created and returns 201, with `failUndispatchedRun` + `run_failed` audit entry (`app/api/runs/route.ts`).\n2. `EngineUnreachableError` timeout vs. generic network failure produce different messages (`lib/server/engine.ts::describe`).\n3. Reviewer approving a conflict with no proposed value (escalated) → 409, distinct from approving an already-resolved one.\n4. Override value that isn't observed on either side → 400 with the exact observed-values list in the message.\n5. `requireReviewer()` throwing when `proxy.ts` and a route handler disagree about auth — should be a loud failure, not swallowed anywhere.\n6. Malformed/non-JSON request bodies on every POST/PATCH route (only the shared `parseJson` helper's happy path is implicitly exercised anywhere; the JSON-parse-failure branch has no test).\n7. `failUndispatchedRun`'s guard: a late dispatch failure must not overwrite a run the engine has already advanced past `queued` — this is a DB-level invariant with no integration test.\n\n### Integration test gaps\n\nThere is currently no integration/e2e layer at all. Given the architecture (Next.js Server Components reading Postgres directly, a separate engine process, Clerk auth), the highest-value integration tests once unit coverage exists would be:\n- A route-handler-level test against a real test Postgres (via `drizzle` + a disposable schema) covering `createRun` → `startRun` failure → `failUndispatchedRun` guard, since that guard's correctness depends on actual row state, not mockable logic.\n- `recordReview` end-to-end against a seeded conflict/resolution row, verifying the audit row's `detail.previousStatus` and that `resolutions.overrideValue` clears correctly across two consecutive reviews of the same conflict.\n- `getQueuePage`/`loadQueue` in `lib/server/conflicts.ts` against seeded data, since its SQL (severity/confidence ordering, NULLS LAST, per-facet count-excluding-self) is exactly the kind of logic that silently breaks under refactors and is invisible to pure unit tests.\n- No browser-level (Playwright) coverage of the review flow (approve/reject/override) or the run-creation flow exists; given `AGENTS.md`'s emphasis on the audit trail as \"the product,\" at least one Playwright smoke test exercising approve→audit-row-appears would catch regressions unit tests can't.\n",
  "parsedOutput": {
    "sections": [
      {
        "title": "Test Coverage Analysis — Canon (web)",
        "content": "\n**Headline finding: this repo has zero test infrastructure.** No test runner is installed (`package.json` has no `jest`/`vitest`/`playwright`/`@testing-library/*`), no `*.test.*`/`*.spec.*` files exist anywhere, and there's no CI test step to enforce coverage going forward. Coverage is 0% across ~30 source files in `lib/`, `lib/server/`, `app/api/`, and `components/`.\n\nBefore anything else, this needs a harness. Recommended: **Vitest** (fast, ESM-native, works well with Next 16 + React 19 Server Components split) + `@testing-library/react` for the handful of client components/hooks. Add:\n\n```bash\nnpm i -D vitest @vitejs/plugin-react @testing-library/react @testing-library/jest-dom jsdom\n```\n\n```ts\n// vitest.config.ts\nimport { defineConfig } from \"vitest/config\";\nimport react from \"@vitejs/plugin-react\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [react()],\n  test: {\n    environment: \"jsdom\",\n    setupFiles: [\"./vitest.setup.ts\"],\n  },\n  resolve: { alias: { \"@\": path.resolve(__dirname, \".\") } },\n});\n```\n\n```json\n// package.json scripts\n\"test\": \"vitest run\",\n\"test:watch\": \"vitest\"\n```\n\nEverything below assumes this setup. Findings are grouped by ROI: pure functions first (no mocking, highest value), then DB-backed server modules, then API routes, then client-side.\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "Tier 1 — Pure functions with zero test coverage (highest ROI)",
        "content": "\nThese have no I/O, are exported, and encode real business rules (survivorship folding, diff rendering, run staging). They should be the first tests written.\n\n| File | Untested exports | Notable edge cases |\n|---|---|---|\n| `lib/validate-value.ts` | `foldValue`, `checkObservedValue`, `observedValues` | multi-suffix stripping (`\"Trellis Labs Pvt Ltd\"`), suffix-only input (`\"Ltd\"`), empty candidate, both sides empty, exact match vs folded match, Unicode normalization (NFKD) |\n| `lib/diff-chars.ts` | `diffSegments` | equal strings, completely disjoint strings, one empty string, prefix+suffix overlap (`\"aa\"` vs `\"a\"`) |\n| `lib/format.ts` | `shortRunId`, `formatElapsed`, `formatCount`, `formatStat`, `formatClockTime`, `formatTimestamp`, `formatRelative`, `formatConfidence` | hour rollover in `formatElapsed`, negative ms, `null`/`undefined` in `formatStat`, boundary seconds in `formatRelative` (59s/60s, 23h/24h) |\n| `lib/rule-trace.ts` | `deriveRuleTrace` | no resolution yet, rule decided vs. model proposed, escalated (no value), rule decided but no strategy found |\n| `lib/reviewer-label.ts` | `reviewerLabel` | null user, username present, only email present, neither present (fallback) |\n| `lib/audit-detail.ts` | `auditDetailParts`, `auditDetailLine`, `auditNote` | empty detail object, `from === to` (no arrow), only `to`, only `from`, unknown `action` (no noun), non-string/non-number malformed detail values |\n| `lib/uuid.ts` | `isUuid` | uppercase UUID, malformed segments, extra characters |\n| `types/queue.ts` | `conflictFieldLabel`, `severityReason` | orphan, duplicate with `to === 0` vs `to > 0`, singular vs plural child count, unknown conflict class (default branch) |\n| `types/run.ts` | `isTerminalRunStatus`, `runStageIndex`, `isStatKnown`, `failedStage`, `RUN_STAGES` | `failed` status (`runStageIndex` → -1), stat not yet produced vs. produced, failed run stat visibility, `failedStage` with no `stage=` in error, case-insensitive verb match, unknown verb |\n| `lib/server/export.ts` | `decisionsToCsv`, `estimateExportBytes`, `isExportSection` | CSV escaping (commas, quotes, newlines in a value), `null` cells, empty decision list |\n\n**Skeletons:**\n\n```ts\n// lib/validate-value.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { foldValue, checkObservedValue, observedValues } from \"@/lib/validate-value\";\n\ndescribe(\"foldValue\", () => {\n  it(\"folds case, punctuation and whitespace\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"ACME-INC\")).toBe(foldValue(\"ACME INC\"));\n  });\n\n  it(\"strips a single legal suffix\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Acme Corp\")).toBe(\"acme\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"strips multiple stacked suffixes, longest match first\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Trellis Labs Pvt Ltd\")).toBe(\"trellis labs\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"keeps a value that IS entirely a suffix\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Ltd\")).toBe(\"ltd\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"is idempotent and total for empty input\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"\")).toBe(\"\");\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"checkObservedValue\", () => {\n  const observed = [\"Acme Inc.\", \"ACME INC\"];\n\n  it(\"accepts an exact match\", () => {\n    const result = checkObservedValue(\"Acme Inc.\", observed);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ ok: true, matches: \"Acme Inc.\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"accepts a legal normalization of an observed value\", () => {\n    const result = checkObservedValue(\"acme inc\", observed);\n    expect(result.ok).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects a value neither side holds\", () => {\n    const result = checkObservedValue(\"Globex\", observed);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ ok: false, reason: expect.stringContaining(\"Must be one of\") });\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects an empty/whitespace-only candidate\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"   \", observed).ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects when neither side has a real value (orphan)\", () => {\n    const result = checkObservedValue(\"anything\", [\"\", \"  \"]);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ ok: false, reason: expect.stringContaining(\"Neither side\") });\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"observedValues\", () => {\n  it(\"flattens and drops blank entries from both sides\", () => {\n    const row = { a: { values: [\"x\", \"\"] }, b: { values: [\"y\"] } };\n    expect(observedValues(row)).toEqual([\"x\", \"y\"]);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```ts\n// types/run.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { isStatKnown, failedStage, runStageIndex, isTerminalRunStatus } from \"@/types/run\";\n\ndescribe(\"isStatKnown\", () => {\n  it(\"is unknown before its producing stage has finished\", () => {\n    expect(isStatKnown(\"matches\", \"extracting\")).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"is known once the producing stage is behind current status\", () => {\n    expect(isStatKnown(\"matches\", \"detecting\")).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  it(\"is known for every stat once complete\", () => {\n    expect(isStatKnown(\"tokensUsed\", \"complete\")).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  it(\"is known for every stat when failed, regardless of where it died\", () => {\n    expect(isStatKnown(\"escalated\", \"failed\")).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"failedStage\", () => {\n  it(\"returns null when the error carries no stage= marker\", () => {\n    expect(failedStage(\"connection reset\")).toBeNull();\n  });\n\n  it(\"maps a known verb to its RunStage, case-insensitively\", () => {\n    expect(failedStage(\"source=Databricks GTM STAGE=Extract\")).toBe(\"extracting\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns null for an unrecognized verb\", () => {\n    expect(failedStage(\"stage=teleport\")).toBeNull();\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns null for a null error\", () => {\n    expect(failedStage(null)).toBeNull();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"runStageIndex / isTerminalRunStatus\", () => {\n  it(\"failed has no position in the pipeline\", () => {\n    expect(runStageIndex(\"failed\")).toBe(-1);\n  });\n\n  it(\"complete and failed are the only terminal states\", () => {\n    expect(isTerminalRunStatus(\"complete\")).toBe(true);\n    expect(isTerminalRunStatus(\"failed\")).toBe(true);\n    expect(isTerminalRunStatus(\"resolving\")).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```ts\n// lib/server/export.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { decisionsToCsv, type DecisionRow } from \"@/lib/server/export\";\n\nconst row: DecisionRow = {\n  conflictId: \"c1\", externalId: \"ACC-1\", entityName: \"Acme, Inc.\", entityType: \"account\",\n  field: \"name\", valueA: \"Acme\", valueB: \"Acme Inc\", conflictClass: \"cosmetic\", severity: 1,\n  detectedBy: \"rule\", status: \"approved\", proposedValue: \"Acme\", overrideValue: null,\n  appliedValue: \"Acme\", appliedRuleId: \"r1\", confidence: 0.9, rationale: \"most_recent\",\n  reviewedBy: \"j.rao\", reviewedAt: \"2026-08-06T18:02:00.000Z\",\n};\n\ndescribe(\"decisionsToCsv\", () => {\n  it(\"quotes and escapes cells containing commas or quotes\", () => {\n    const csv = decisionsToCsv([row]);\n    expect(csv).toContain('\"Acme, Inc.\"');\n  });\n\n  it(\"emits a header row plus CRLF-terminated rows, ending with a trailing CRLF\", () => {\n    const csv = decisionsToCsv([row]);\n    expect(csv.endsWith(\"\\r\\n\")).toBe(true);\n    expect(csv.split(\"\\r\\n\")[0]).toContain(\"conflictId\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"renders null cells as empty strings, not the literal 'null'\", () => {\n    const csv = decisionsToCsv([{ ...row, overrideValue: null }]);\n    expect(csv).not.toContain(\"null\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"handles an empty decision list (header only)\", () => {\n    expect(decisionsToCsv([]).trim().split(\"\\r\\n\")).toHaveLength(1);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
